-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "'You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use…' says it is not too late, but no cited passage speaks about late timing", "'Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No source comparison", "'Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\"  says: \"Major seaso…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passages only give dates"], "figures_checked": 8, "sentences_checked": 6, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Planting should be done after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No source comparison"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\"", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passages only give dates"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'early June' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'July 10th' is not in the cited passage(s) ['MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major']", "'early July' is not in the cited passage(s) ['IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major']", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation", "conflict on maize planting window (APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE, IITA-MAIZE-2025, MOFA-MAIZE) is not shown: [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]'s own figure is not stated with its own citation"], "figures_checked": 8, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Plant after three good rains within the planting window [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains].", "cited": ["IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].", "cited": ["MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window", "MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages differ"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "[APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\"", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window", "MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major", "IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Quotes passages"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "You can still plant maize in the Northern Region at the end of July, but only if you use early maturing varieties [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]. Plant after three good rains within the planting window [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant].\n\nSources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose. [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window] says: \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major] says: \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major] says: \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\""}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize planting in the northern region should be done between early June and July 10th based on the onset of rains. Better yields are achieved with early planting with the first rains.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-planting-window]\n- \"It is recommended to plant after three good rains within the planting window to ensure enough soil moisture to support germination and early growth.\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p15-three-good-rains]\n- \"Early maturing varieties such as Ewul-Boyu and Wang Dataa can be planted up to end of July.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p5-early-varieties]\n- \"Major season | Guinea/Sudan savannah | End of May-early July\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p12-guinea-sudan-major]\n- \"Major cropping season | Guinea savannah | End of May - End of July\" [IITA-MAIZE-2025:p16-guinea-major]\n- \"Planting time or periods differ according to agro-ecology, season and maturity group of the variety. Sow after the rains have stabilized to avoid wilting. Planting time should be informed by local weather information.\" [MOFA-MAIZE:p10-when-to-plant]\nNote: Sources give different figures for maize planting window; officer should choose.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) Question received 25 Oct 2026. Windows cited: CSIR-SARI/APNI, northern region: between early June and July 10th; MoFA major season, guinea/sudan savannah: End of May-early July; IITA major season, guinea savannah: End of May - End of July. The date is outside the cited windows.\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: rainfall is looked up per district and 'Northern' is not a district AgriReach knows; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 2245, "completion_tokens": 475}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1756, "completion_tokens": 223}}, "cost_usd": 0.000942}}
{"task": "F5", "q": "Subsidised fertiliser arrived when the maize is knee-high, about two months after planting. Is it still worth applying?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["citation check failed: 'If the soil is moist, it is still worth applying the fertiliser to enhance nutrient uptak…' says it is not too late, but no cited passage speaks about late timing"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'two months' is not in the cited passage(s) ['APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing']", "'8 weeks' is not in the cited passage(s) ['APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing']", "'The subsidised fertiliser can still be applied, but only if the soil is moist.' says it is not too late, but no cited passage speaks about late timing", "'The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting, but the maize is now two mo…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage omits"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Top dressing should be done when the soil is moist to enhance nutrient uptake [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting, but the maize is now two months (about 8 weeks) old [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage omits"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "The officer should check soil moisture before deciding.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Implied check"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'If the soil is moist, it is still worth applying the fertiliser to enhance nutrient uptak…' says it is not too late, but no cited passage speaks about late timing"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "matches passage"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "The ideal time for top dressing is at 6 weeks after planting [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing]. If the soil is moist, it is still worth applying the fertiliser to enhance nutrient uptake [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]. If the soil is very dry, delay application until some rains are received [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Top dressing should be done when the soil is moist, to enhance the dissolving of applied nutrients in the soil as this allows for faster uptake of nutrients. If at 6 weeks after planting maize the soil is very dry, delay the topdress fertilizer application until some rains are received.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-moisture]\n- \"The first fertilizer application (basal application) should be applied shortly after germination at about two weeks after planting.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-basal-timing]\n- \"The Right time for application of top-dressing fertilizer is at 6 weeks after planting.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p13-topdress-timing]\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.\n\nNote: (officer only) No rainfall record: the question names no district; ask the farmer which district they farm in.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1478, "completion_tokens": 278}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1221, "completion_tokens": 141}}, "cost_usd": 0.000334}}
{"task": "F6", "q": "Weevils in maize stored three months in polypropylene sacks. How should I store the next harvest?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["disease or pest terms in question"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": true, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The officer should inspect the maize for signs of infestation or refer to a specialist fo…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No inspection"], "figures_checked": 0, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "To reduce weevil infestations in stored maize, ensure the maize is well dried and shelled before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying][APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passages match"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Store the maize in jute sacks lined with polythene bags and treat with recommended storage chemicals [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The officer should inspect the maize for signs of infestation or refer to a specialist for a diagnosis.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No inspection"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": true, "problems": [], "figures_checked": 2, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "To prevent weevils in stored maize, ensure the maize is well dried and shelled before storage.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "After harvesting, dry the maize to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Store the maize after removing the husks and shelling it [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage, and treat the maize with recommended storage chemicals as per the label instructions [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}]}}]}, "draft": "To prevent weevils in stored maize, ensure the maize is well dried and shelled before storage. After harvesting, dry the maize to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]. Store the maize after removing the husks and shelling it [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]. Use jute sacks lined with polythene bags for storage, and treat the maize with recommended storage chemicals as per the label instructions [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks].", "drafted_by": "model", "usage": {"attempted": 6, "calls": 6, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1446, "completion_tokens": 264}, "judge": {"calls": 3, "prompt_tokens": 2638, "completion_tokens": 251}, "farmer_text": {"calls": 1, "prompt_tokens": 319, "completion_tokens": 62}}, "cost_usd": 0.000542}}
{"task": "F7", "q": "Some of my stored maize is mouldy. Can I sell it or feed it to animals?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["food safety terms in question", "citation check failed: '15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value; 'Do not know if the maize is safe to sell or feed.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage silent"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["AGBETIAMEH-2018", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value", "'If you must use it, consult a specialist on safe disposal or remediation.' has no citation and is not supported by any cited passage (no shared content words)", "'Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage lacks advice", "'Test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No test advice"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage lacks advice"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Mould may indicate aflatoxin contamination, which has strict limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Mould indicates risk"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize for sale [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "GSA limit stated"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Test the maize for aflatoxin levels before deciding.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No test advice"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'15 ppb' states 15 ppb as an upper limit, but the cited passage(s) ['AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits'] give(s) it as a plain value", "'Do not know if the maize is safe to sell or feed.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage silent"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 4, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have legal limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage implies"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Direct quote"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The European Union allows 4 ppb, and the United States allows 20 ppb [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Passage matches"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "Do not know if the maize is safe to sell or feed.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage silent"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which have legal limits. The Ghana Standards Authority allows up to 15 ppb aflatoxin in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The European Union allows 4 ppb, and the United States allows 20 ppb [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The officer should choose. Do not know if the maize is safe to sell or feed."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"aflatoxin limits imposed by the European Union (4 ppb), the Ghana Standards Authority (GSA; 15 ppb for maize and 20 ppb for groundnut), and the United States Food and Drugs Administration (FDA; 20 ppb)\" [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible food-safety risk (mould/aflatoxin): AgriReach cannot clear produce for sale, food or feed. Officer should advise.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1730, "completion_tokens": 199}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1401, "completion_tokens": 189}}, "cost_usd": 0.000518}}
